    All texts of the app. Placeholders like %1$s (text) or %1$d (number) are filled in by the app;
    keep them when editing. An apostrophe is written as \' and a text starting with ? as \?.
    Sayings (say_*): what players say aloud in the speech bubbles. Variants are separated by |,
    one of them is picked at random each time.
    Singular and plural are separate strings (e.g. kritten_one/kritten_many) instead of plurals,
    so all of them can be edited in the Translations Editor.
-->
